==Appearance==
<tabber>
|-|Default=
Squirm is a bookworm [[Toon]] with six body segments, which alternates in color between blue and dark mint. He features antennae on top of his head, which are also colored mint. The second segment of his body is shaped like a dewlap, while the third, fourth, and fifth segments of his body have a pair of limbs, specifically two arms and four thick bipedal legs. The final sixth segment is a slightly smaller, curved blob, functioning as a tail. His limbs are a greenish-yellowish color, the same color as the heart shaped part of his face. He also has three spots along both sides of each section, interchanging mint to blue, with the first appearing as freckles, being situated closer to his cheeks. His facial expression consists of droopy eyes, often with a squiggly frown on his face. His design is very caterpillar like, which leads him to believing he is one himself.
|-|Vintage=
Vintage Squirm's eyes are pie-cut to the left and his colors are replaced with grayscale hues, with his blue being dark gray, his green-yellow being light gray, his freckles being black, and his other mint colors being a medium gray.
|-|Spring Quilt=
Spring Quilt Squirm is recolored from blue to a pastel yellow, mint to a pastel pink, and green-yellow to a lighter butter yellow. A pastel green bow tie featuring a white knot and pair of tails with two rounded ends is positioned below his dewlap. He now wears a light pink flower with five petals and a yellow center on the right of his forehead, while a smaller, reversely colored flower rests on the left of his second layer. He also wears a checkered, light lime and pink quilt on his back, spread with three pink flowers and two yellow ones, varying in size.
|-|Reluctant Rocker=
Reluctant Rocker Squirm's blue, dark mint, and lime green hues are respectively swapped out for pistachio green, grayish-teal, and deep blue, with the exception of his heart-shaped face marking, covered in white face paint, and his antennae which are deep blue instead of grayish-teal. The dots on his sides are now triangular, and the first pair is no longer visible, being coated over. He has shiny, bright green eyeshadow and black mascara under his eyes, giving him a pair of visible, sharp eyelashes. There are neon green spikes along his backside, with there being three on his first and fifth segments and one on his tail. On both arms, he wears black bracelets with four spikes similar to the aforementioned ones, as well as a black shirt with a jagged hem and set of sleeves.
|-|Web Weaver=
Web Weaver Squirm is a slightly pinkish shade of brown with darker antennae and limbs, a lighter face, third segment, and fifth segment, and an even lighter second layer. The dots on his first and seconds layers are removed, while the remaining are lighter dots with the darker layers and vice versa. He has a fanged frown, and two red bumps on his forehead and on each of his cheeks, with the cheeks' being slightly smaller. He wears a dark brown cape with a red hourglass on it and two spider-like arms that are attached to his real arms by black strings.
</tabber>

==Personality==
Squirm can be described as pessimistic, anxious, and openly self-deprecating. He can be seen as immature, though in a much more saddening way, compared to most other Toons' spirited or composed attitudes. He has persistent anxiety which can go as far to the point of even screaming and/or crying if he gets very emotional, expressed by his tendency to sniffle a lot during his elevator interactions with other [[Toons]] and his own dialogues when descending to another [[Floor]]. He's also known to get awkward at moments, like when he gets a hug from {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, or invited to scrapbook with {{CI|Flyte|name=true}}.

As seen by his interaction with {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}, Squirm describes himself as "useless", nearing tears most of the time when he gets even slightly upset and even agrees with {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}} in their dialogue together when Shrimpo berates him. It's also notable that he has an appetite for books, which could be the reason he is banned from {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}'s book club (mentioned in their dialogue), and also that eating books is his coping mechanism. Squirm is also extremely sensitive, especially to inadvertent insults; shown in his conversation with {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}.

Aside from the surface, he appears to have a crisis involving his identity, as seen in his interaction with {{CI|Flutter|name=true}} and {{CI|Dyle|name=true}}'s [[Gossip]] about him. He sees himself as a caterpillar, with Flutter being implied to agree with this (likely due to her also being an insect from the {{wp|lepidoptera}} order), however he was assigned as a bookworm by {{CI|Arthur|name=true}}, believing that a "bookworm" is a type of worm rather than larvae. Shrimpo additionally insults him for not looking like a worm, which seems to only amplify his identity conflict.

Squirm seems to be hesitant in doing things he's not certain of, this proves to be a fact with his interaction with {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}. Because he is always so tense, Squirm also can overthink things. This proves to be a fact with his dialogues when descending to another Floor, where he tends to think the floors will introduce greater threats and his interaction with {{CI|Looey|name=true}}.

