==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, you need to walk under {{CI|Twisted Squirm|name=true}} and get caught by him to obtain [[Research]]. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting it faster because of his Passive [[Ability]]. This will be easier if Twisted Squirm is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*For the second requirement, you will need to complete 3 [[Achievements]] and redeem its Medal in order to get its Title. It is recommended to get 3 of any Bronze Achievements as they are the easiest to get.
*For the third requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.

==Strategies==
Squirm is considerably one of the best non-{{Type|Main}} and non-[[Event]] extractors in the game, having 5{{Star}} [[Extraction Speed]] alongside an average 3 Star in [[Skill Check]].

With his Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Squirm|name=true}}, Squirm can be considered the best extractor in the game. His Ability significantly increases the speed he completes a [[Machine]] (doubling his Extraction Speed), making the usual 25.2 second average of Machine completion time go down to an average of 17.53. For the full 10 second duration of his Ability's boost, 30 units of a Machine will be filled. While this makes him the fastest extractor in the game, do note it has a cooldown, hence why a Squirm player should likely stay close to bookshelves around the map, as they make his cooldown deplete twice as fast. This also means he has advantages in certain maps, specifically the [[Library Floor]] or [[Rainbow Rooms]]. However, maps with less bookshelves, especially the [[Diner]] [[Floors]] and [[Sprout's Floor]] (some of the Diner variants and Sprout's Floor have none), can be less beneficial for Squirm. However, do not waste your time finding and idling next to bookshelves if you don't see the need to do so. By default you’d have to idle by a bookshelf for 40 seconds to fully reduce his cooldown, with one/both cooldown reducing cards you’d have to idle for 37.5/35 seconds respectively. Thus, try to stick by bookshelves for only a fraction of that time, unless all other Machines are currently being extracted. Generally, only idle by bookshelves if you are sure your team has a Machine left for you, and even so, Squirm's normal Extraction Speed is still more than fine. It is possible to eat some bookshelves from the side or back, as well as through certain walls, meaning you are able to hide from [[Twisteds]] or distractors while reducing your cooldown.  Also, note that if you just use his Ability right as you go on a Machine, by the time Squirm's Extraction boost wears off, you are most likely done with the Machine, so refrain from using it midway unless you are afflicted with {{Debuff|Confused}} or otherwise hindered extraction-wise.

Squirm's main disadvantages are his Stealth and Stamina, both of which can cause trouble when escaping Twisteds or trying to avoid distractors. Though there aren't many ways to mitigate his Stealth, issues with his Stamina can be dulled with the {{CDI|Well-Paced/Endurance|name=true}} [[Cards]], as well as completing {{CDI|TIME'S UP}}[[Dyle's Floor]], and, though not recommended, using [[Trinkets]] like {{TI|Cooler|name=true}} or {{TI|Speedometer|name=true}}. Though below average, his Statistics are never too big of an issue unless in certain situations, so the best recommendation is to keep notice of where you are going or what dangers are near you in order to be safer. It is also worth noting that winding up his Ability will decrease his [[Movement Speed]] by 50% or half (7.5 Walk Speed/12.5 Run Speed), thus it is important to be cautious with when you wind it up, especially if there are ranged Twisteds or fast Twisteds on the Floor; you'd delay your reaction, which can prevent you from breaking line of sight fast enough to avoid damage or using up excess Stamina.

Good [[Items]] to focus on are those related to mobility. Stamina Items like {{II|Pop|name=false|plural=a}} and {{II|Protein Bar|name=false|plural=a}} especially can help maintain Squirm's below average Stamina, especially since he relies on it quite a bit with his average speed. Movement Speed boosting Items can help with escaping from Twisteds, reducing the need to use his Stamina somewhat. Extraction related Items like {{II|Instructions|name=false}} and {{II|Skill Check Candy|name=false|plural=a}} can make his high extraction even better, especially if they boost Extraction Speed, since that can stack with his Ability. Infact, you can use Instructions as a stand-in for his Ability if it's on cooldown.

Overall, Squirm is a great extractor Toon with little to no downsides, making him a great pick for those who desire to have a great Extraction experience.

