==Trivia==
*The word Squirm means to wriggle the body side-to-side, referencing Squirm being a worm-like animal.
**Additionally, in some definitions, the wriggling comes from nervousness, discomfort, or mostly any negative emotions, something that likely references Squirm's distressed personality.
**The word 'Worm' could be heard when pronouncing Squirm, something that, again, parallels with Squirm being a book worm.
*Squirm is the first [[Toon]] to be released in 2026.
*Squirm is the first [[Toon]] to cry in his dialogues, and the first character to do so overall.
**Although {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle}}[[Dazzle]] appears to be crying, it is more than likely either makeup or a natural part of his appearance.
*Despite looking like a caterpillar, which is a part of a {{wp|lepidoptera}}'s life cycle, Squirm is in fact a book worm, not related to {{CI|Flutter|name=true}} and {{CI|Flyte|name=true}},<ref>https://discordapp.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1474917227240231046</ref> and is an adult.<ref>https://discordapp.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1474916246809219092</ref> 
**Interestingly, his {{CI|Twisted Squirm}}[[Twisted Squirm|Twisted counterpart]] can be seen inside of a cocoon, which is the third stage of a lepidoptera's life cycle.
***The term "book worm" is a metaphor/umbrella term for insects or larva that eat/damage books (or less commonly, wood in general), including certain moth caterpillars. Thus, it is possible that he is in fact a caterpillar, or of a moth specifically.
**In his interaction with Flutter and {{CI|Dyle|name=true}}'s [[Gossip]] about him, it might be implied Squirm is actually a caterpillar or just believes that he is one, despite being told by [[Arthur]] that he is a book worm, meaning he's probably one in name only.
*Squirm is the first [[Toon]] to receive their first [[Stickers]] that were not made by [[Qwel]], instead made by [[Ramblesnake]].
*Squirm is the first [[Toon]] to have an [[Ability]] that can affect and interact with a decoration on some [[Floors]].
*Squirm used to be in {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}'s book club, but was likely kicked for eating books. Brightney catching him at the library as shown on the thumbnail and reveal video is what was implied to have lead to this.
**However, they seem to still be on good terms, and Brightney tries to help him manage his stress and compulsive book eating.
*Squirm appears to be good friends with [[Flutter]], who he spends time with and who agrees with his identity as a caterpillar rather than a bookworm. He’s also friends with [[Dazzle]] (and possibly Razzle), who he finds comfort in being around and wants to "catch up" with after his banning from the book club, missing their time spent together. [[Flyte]] also appears to be good friends with him, as they act very friendly towards eachother, and Flyte suggests scrapbooking with him.
*Squirm can eat one of six books when using his [[Ability]], five being based on a {{Type|Main}} and one being based on {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}. These books are {{CI|Astro|name=true}} Bedtime Stories, Dandy Stories, {{CI|Pebble}}[[Pebble|Pet Rock]] Care Guide, {{CI|Shelly}}[[Shelly|Fossils]], {{CI|Sprout}}[[Sprout|Cook Book]], and {{CI|Vee|name=true}}-[[Vee-Mail|Mail]] Console. There's also an additional book that's simply named "Squirm".
**In the [[Lobby]] and [[Roleplay Mode]], the book model uses a unique texture, being a lavender book with a light blue spine, and a drawing of Squirm on it with his name underneath.
*Squirm is the second [[Toon]] to have 6 limbs, the first being [[Astro]].
**Contrasting Astro's 4 arms and 2 legs, Squirm has 4 legs and 2 arms.
*Squirm is the first [[Toon]] who can decrease the cooldown time of their [[Ability]] without the need of [[Trinkets]] or [[Cards]].
*Squirm is the second [[Toon]] with an Active [[Ability]] that requires a wind-up period before it is activated, the first being {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}.
**However, Squirm is the first Toon whose Ability was always this way, as Ginger's Ability was reworked in [[Changelog|v0.14.1]].
**Squirm is also the first Toon whose wind-up prerequisite Ability doesn't require [[Tapes]] to work and only affects himself instead of others.
*It is implied Squirm is very stressed likely caused by an identity crisis as hinted in Dyle's [[Gossip]] on him. His stress is also shown with his {{TI|Stress Ball|name=true}} [[Trinket]] being burst open due to the amount stress Squirm is under, stress-eating books as seen in multiple interactions, and in his dialogue and interactions, he has a negativity bias and thinks of what else could go wrong and thinks of the worst possible outcome.
**That, his book obsession, Gardenview shutting down, eating other people's books and being kicked out of the Book Club likely just amplified his stress.
*On his release, Squirm had 30% [[Skill Check]] Chance and 135 Skill Check Size.<ref>[[File:Squirm_Stats_v16.6.jpeg|200px]]<br>'''NOTE:''' Skill Check chance and size was modified with {{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}, hence why it's 55% Skill Check chance. Also, this was during a time where the 10% size decrease wasn't working for Participation Award, hence the 135 couldn't come from Participation Award</ref> Somewhere after his release, his Skill Check Chance was changed back to 25%.
**A similar bug has happened with {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, who had 20% Skill Check Chance upon release, [[Bassie]], who had 150 Skill Check Size, and {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, who had 50% Skill Check Chance, all upon their initial release.
*Squirm is the only one of the 4 recent base-toons ({{CI|Blot|name=true}}, {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, and {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}}) that has at least one dialogue with all the other base-toons since his release.
*Squirm is the eighth non-[[Main Character]] [[Toon]] to have 5{{Star}} on a stat.
*Squirm is the fourth [[Toon]] to be released by himself.
*Squirm is the first [[Toon]] to have 2 [[Floor]] Dialogues, with one on the [[Library Floor]] in his Jr. Reading Nook area, and the other being in the [[Gift Shop]] in the Trading Card area.
*On the texture of the book pages when Squirm is eating a book or a bookshelf, the pages are all the same, and seem to be a poem from the game called "STILL GOING", which reads:
**"The caterpillar was always late. When it tried to climb, it fell. When it dreamed of flying, someone laughed. While the others moved on, it stayed behind, thinking it was made wrong. One day it built its cocoon. It broke. Like everything else. But from the ground, for the first time, no one was looking down on it. When it came out, it didn't fly high. Or beautifully. But it kept going. And for it, that was enough."
**The poem seems to be about how Squirm became a [[Twisted Squirm|Twisted]] with no one looking down on him, since he is on the ceiling, how Twisted Squirm is in a broken cocoon, wasn't given the ability to fly, and did not become "beautiful" after he came out.
***It is possible Squirm tried to form a cocoon at some point, but likely got attacked by another Twisted or some other means, which caused him to turn twisted.
*Squirm's favorite pie is apple pie, as mentioned in his interaction with [[Sprout]].
*If you haven't redeemed a title in the [[Journal]] yet and go to the Titles section, there will be a sticky note reading "Did Squirm eat them?".<ref>[[File:Titles Page.png|250px]]</ref>
*Squirm is the third [[Toon]] to be an insect, the first being [[Flutter]], and the second being [[Flyte]].
**He is the only one who doesn't have the letter "F" in the start of his name. This is because Flutter and Flyte's names relate to how a butterfly flies, as well as referencing a group (a group of butterflies is called both a "flutter" and a "flight"), whilst Squirm's name refers to a motion that caterpillars generally do.
**Coincidentally, they are all a member of {{wp|lepidoptera}}.
*Squirm is the first [[Toon]] to have an [[Achievement]] dedicated to them, that being {{TTI|Fine Dining|name=true}}.
*Squirm is the first and currently only [[Toon]] to have the letter Q in their name.
*Weirdly, when you put Squirm next to a bookshelf and he starts eating, the texture of the bookshelf makes it seem as though he ate the spines of the bookshelf makes, rather than eating one whole book at a time like in his [[Ability]] animation.
*Squirm and [[Yatta]] share some similarities.
**They have almost the same [[Stat]] spread, only Squirm has lower Movement Speed and higher Stamina.
**They have an [[Ability]] that gives a boost (Yatta's candies do this indirectly), relates to extracting, and technically interacts with the map around them (Yatta's candies spawn around her when she finishes a [[Machine]] or gets attacked, and Squirm eats bookshelves to lower his cooldown).
**They were the first base-game Toons to release in their respective years.
**They had incorrect Skill Checks values on release.
**They cost a large amount of {{TI|Ichor|name=true}}, need 50% on their [[Twisted]] counterparts, and require you to own something.
***Ironically, their personalities contrast, with Yatta being hyper and positive, while Squirm is more distressed and negative.
*For some reason, Squirm's [[Ability]] gives 5 {{TI|Tapes|name=true}} every time the Ability is used successfully, instead of the usual 3 on the first use of the Floor. This means that Squirm can basically farm Tapes very easily by earning 5 every 40-80 seconds.
*Squirm is the third [[Toon]] with an atypical body shape (not default, chubby, or slim), the first being [[Pebble]], and the second being {{CI|Coal|name=true}}.
*When eating from a bookshelf while having {{Debuff|Ignited}}, Squirm's cooldown will speed up by 4x instead of 2x, with the graphic also showing "x4".
*Squirm and {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}} have some similarities.
**They have new letters no other [[Toons]] have in their name.
**They both frequently show negative emotions, with Waxwell being "malice" and Squirm being distressed.
**They have 5 Stars on an Extracting [[Stat]].
**Their Twisteds are '''{{Type|Rare}}'''s.
**Both require 50% [[Research]] of their Twisted counterparts to obtain.
**They both have 2 Stars in [[Stealth]].
**They were released in 2026.
**They have the ability to speed up an [[Ability]]'s cooldown by 2 times.
**They had prior teasers that showed a vague sense of what they were (Squirm's silhouette and Waxwell's candlewick), before getting a short that fully revealed them a few days before their releases.
*Weirdly, all [[Ability]] warning messages (like being in cooldown or in the [[Elevator]]) are displayed similarly to [[Research]] text for Squirm rather than the regular text next to the Ability button.
